# Not screens: the competition creators of the key nation entries (G_LEAGUE_TABLE rows), called through
# KEY_NATION_RECORD_SETUP_FUNC by key_nation_create_all_comps 0x669180 (create_game) for the international rows and
# the nations with a selected league. Uses the mould of tel13_2: goes after it.
# Conventions checked in the disassembly and at the call site (0x6691a7: push ecx; call eax; add esp, 4): cdecl(entry)
# -> 1 or 0, ret 0; operator new 0x944cf1 and calloc 0x945501 cdecl; every constructor thiscall(this, year dword,
# competition record) ret 8 (checked: the first ret of each is ret 8); Date::Date 0x549f70 thiscall ret 0x10;
# Date::add_weeks 0x54c770 thiscall(date, out, 4) ret 8; key_nation_continent_has_selected_nation 0x6699d0 cdecl.
# Each routine was emulated (unicorn) from the original bytes with marked inputs (game year, start year, the nation's
# extra division bit, the continent answer) and the data of its KeyNationComps were taken from what it wrote: the
# entry's fields, the calloc arguments, each new size, constructor and its arguments and the slot.
# The year dword a constructor gets: the original pushes a dword whose high word is stack leftover (the year word
# was stored into a local); the copy zero-extends it (the constructors read the word). Brazil's is the dword of its
# date from the year on, as the original.
# Which run in the automatic career (ENG, auto_setup.cfg; once, in create_game): create_english_comps; with the 8
# leagues also create_french_comps, create_italian_comps and create_japanese_comps; the others only with their leagues chosen.
# DEFECTS of the original kept: see tel13_2 (the copied allocation messages, the untouched LEAGUE_COMP of Poland and Wales).
